The code in this repository is covered by the licence above. Two things in it are not:

  * The Ministry of Health data the models were trained on is open data distributed to GovTech Camp 2026
    participants by the organisers. It is not included in the repository (see docs/raw-manifest.json for what was
    used and docs/data.md for how it is processed); its own terms of use apply.

  * The published evidence under seed/ (forecasts, signals, stress tests, the model passport) is derived from that
    data. It is committed so the product can be started and checked, and it carries the limitations documented in
    docs/model-assurance-6b5.md. It describes a retrospective origin (2025-03-17) and must not be presented as a
    current picture of any hospital.

The system supports human decisions and takes none: every capability in the model passport is recorded with
human_review_required = true and autonomous_action = false.
